# Cite the software. ORCIDs are omitted rather than filled with placeholders —
# they go in once registered. The JOSS DOI and a `preferred-citation` block for
# the paper go in on acceptance.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this viewer in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Retina Tomography Viewer"
abstract: >-
  A zero-install browser viewer for segmented ocular micro-computed-tomography.
  Two linked 3D panes show a reference eye and the segmented tissue layers of a
  scan, with per-structure visibility, tri-planar slicing with solid caps, and
  camera synchronisation. The rendering core is a DOM-free ES module library
  that also runs headless under Node.
type: software
authors:
